    "body": "Reference check (per maintainer rule: maintainer-filed claims verified against public documentation; no other product's code or output).\n\nConfirms: vertices/corners are documented selectable WCS-origin points - the Setup reference's \"Selected point\" origin offers \"a vertex or an edge\" ([Fusion CAM Setup reference](https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/ENU/Fusion-CAM/files/MFG-REF-SETUP-MILL.htm)).\nContradicts: nothing directly, but the cited docs do not list face-edge midpoints or circle/slot centres as standard origin snaps; placing an origin at an arbitrary point is documented via a sketch point workaround ([origin that does not show up](https://www.autodesk.com/support/technical/article/caas/sfdcarticles/sfdcarticles/How-to-select-the-WCS-Origin-that-does-not-show-up-in-the-stock-box-points.html)) - so \"centres available to pick\" is a convenience beyond the documented baseline, which this repo already ships for feature points/circle centres (PR #1405).\nUnclear: which snap set a given CAM dialog exposes varies; no public standard fixes the exact list. Expanding to solid vertices alongside the current edge midpoints matches the documented behaviour.\n",
